# Sanad Vercel production

- **Production URL:** https://sanad-five-zeta.vercel.app/ (also `.cursor/sanad-production.url`)
- **Vercel project:** `sanad-five-zeta` on Vercel

When the user asks to deploy or redeploy after changes:

1. Commit/push only when the user explicitly asks.
2. Read Vercel credentials from the user's **personal agent store** file `sanad-vercel-deploy.json` (never commit tokens; never paste tokens in chat).
3. Deploy with `VERCEL_TOKEN` set from that store, from project root: `npx vercel deploy --prod` (link project first with `npx vercel link` if `.vercel` is missing).
4. Confirm production env vars on Vercel match Supabase (`NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, service role server-only).

Local dev uses `.env.local`; production uses Vercel environment variables.
